    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW29t5EaomezaybhY3pTv6Nu9)_\n\n## Summary\n- New module `sp-vulpea-meta-order` (docs/tangles/vulpea/sp-vulpea-meta-order.org):\n  - `sp-vulpea-meta-order-keys` / `-sorted-p` order any list of meta keys; `-buffer` / `-string` order the first `- key :: value` list of a note.\n  - Only that list moves: items keep their continuation lines, repeated keys keep their order, text outside is untouched, a sorted list is not rewritten (idempotent).\n  - `sp-vulpea-meta-order-pinned` (default nil) can keep chosen keys first.\n  - `M-x sp-vulpea-meta-order-note` for the current note.\n  - `M-x sp-vulpea-meta-order-dryrun` / `-convert` for existing Vulpea notes: shared `sp-batch-report-mode` buffer (d/u/A/g), tag and folder filter (options, or prefix arg), time-stamped backups, one confirmation, unsaved buffers skipped. No old-interface view (new commands).\n- `sp-litnotes-meta-fill` now orders the meta lines (result lists `\"order\"`), so the batch `-fill-all-convert` does too. The dry run plans and reports \"order the meta lines\". `sp-litnotes-meta-order-meta` (default t) turns it off.\n- Not changed: meta lists under headings; no CHANGELOG edits.\n\n## Testing\n- ERT: new `tests/sp-vulpea-meta-order-test.el` (12), `sp-litnotes-meta-test.el` (28), batch-report and convert-properties tests pass on Emacs 29 with stubbed Vulpea. Not run on the real vault.\n\nBranch could not be renamed with the PR number from the cloud session.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCNr5CyTzUFEABVLfb)_",
